  "about": "The resolver contract, one row per situation. 'world' is a tiny invented knowledge base: each name is an entity, 'sources' are the files (numbered) that mention it. 'deleted' names are tombstones. A case asks the resolver about 'text' in 'query' mode (a name written in a question, inside the files of 'selection'; leave it out for no restriction) or in 'ingestion' mode (a name read in a file; 'in_source' lists the entities already seen in that same file; leave it out when unknown). 'outcome' is existing, possible_match, ambiguous, new_entity or unresolved; 'who' the names it must point at (any order); 'reason' the code of a possible match or of an unresolved answer. Add a row, run `cargo test --test knowledge_resolver the_resolver_cases_hold -- --nocapture`, and read the table. A phonetic key is never written here: two names either sound alike to the encoder or they do not.",
